===Etymology===
{{suffix|de|Eichhorn|-chen}}, diminutive of {{m|de|Eichhorn}}, folk etymology based on {{m|de|Eiche}} and {{m|de|Horn}}, but actually from {{der|de|goh|eihhorno}}, from {{der|de|gem-pro|*aikwernô}}, ultimately from {{der|de|ine-pro|*aig-||move quickly}}, cognate with {{cog|ang|acol||frightened}} and {{cog|ine-pro|*wer-||squirrel}}.<ref>{{R:Duden}}</ref><ref>{{R:DWDS}}</ref> Compare {{cog|nl|eekhoorn}}, {{m|nl|eekhoorntje}}, {{cog|fy|iikhoarntsje}}, {{cog|enm|aquerne}}, {{cog|da|egern}}, {{cog|nb|ekorn}}, {{cog|sv|ekorre}}, {{cog|is|íkorni}}.

